From: DHB_AX local port <local@invalid>
Subject: [LOCAL ONLY] net: stmmac: report the RX descriptor low-water mark

On a receive engine that cannot be restarted once it suspends for want of
a descriptor, the measurement that matters is how close the ring came to
empty, and nothing in the driver reports it.  RU says the ring did run
out; below that threshold there is no reading at all.

An external sampler cannot supply one either.  At 30k packets per second a
256-entry ring empties in under nine milliseconds, so a poller fast enough
to see the approach would have to run faster than the fault it is
measuring.

Latch the minimum in the receive path instead.  The descriptors the DMA
still owns run from the one it is working on, which CSR19 reports, to the
oldest the driver has yet to hand back; cur_rx and dirty_rx describe only
the driver's own progress and cannot answer this between them.  Read CSR19
through a new DMA operation, sample once per NAPI poll at the point the
ring is emptiest -- after the poll has consumed descriptors and before the
refill returns them -- and expose the minimum as ethtool -S
rx_desc_low_water.

The figure covers the interval since the last read and is a single value
across receive queues, which is exact for a one-queue instance.  A read
reports the interval that ends and starts the next.
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/common.h b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/common.h
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/common.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/common.h
@@ -143,6 +143,8 @@ struct stmmac_extra_stats {
 	unsigned long rx_overflow_cntr;
 	unsigned long rx_vlan;
 	unsigned long rx_split_hdr_pkt_n;
+	/* Rx descriptor ring pressure, reset on read */
+	unsigned long rx_desc_low_water;
 	/* Tx/Rx IRQ error info */
 	unsigned long tx_undeflow_irq;
 	unsigned long tx_process_stopped_irq;
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac1000_dma.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac1000_dma.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac1000_dma.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac1000_dma.c
@@ -266,6 +266,14 @@ static int dwmac1000_get_hw_feature(void __iomem *ioaddr,
